        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>SCHEDULE A, PART IV, SECTION D, LINE 2</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE FOUNDATION HOLDS BI-MONTHLY BOARD MEETINGS, AND THE SCHOOL'S PRINCIPAL ATTENDS ALL BOARD MEETINGS. ADDITIONALLY, TWO TEACHER LIASONS ATTEND BOARD MEETINGS. THIS IS HOW THE FOUNDATION MAINTAINS A CLOSE AND CONTINUOUS WORKING RELATIONSHIP WITH THE SCHOOL. SEE ALSO THE RESPONSE BELOW TO SECTION D, LINE 3, FOR ADDITIONAL INFORMATION.</ExplanationTxt>
      </Form990ScheduleAPartVIGrp>
      <Form990ScheduleAPartVIGrp>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>SCHEDULE A, PART IV, SECTION D, LINE 3</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>ALTHOUGH THE SCHOOL PRINCIPAL IS NOT A VOTING MEMBER OF THE BOARD, THE PRINCIPAL PROVIDES INPUT AT THE BOARD MEETINGS ON SCHOOL NEEDS AND MAKES REQUESTS FOR FUNDING FROM THE FOUNDATION FOR SPECIFIC PURPOSES.</ExplanationTxt>
      </Form990ScheduleAPartVIGrp>
      <Form990ScheduleAPartVIGrp>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>SCHEDULE A, PART IV, SECTION E, LINE 2A</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE FOUNDATION WAS ESTABLISHED IN 2005 TO SPECIFICALLY BENEFIT ONLY MCKINLEY ELEMENTARY SCHOOL. ALL FUNDRAISING EFFORTS AND PROGRAM SERVICE GRANTS BENEFIT MCKINLEY ELEMENTARY SCHOOL. SEE FORM 990, PART III, FOR THE VARIOUS PROGRAM SERVICES PROVIDED TO ENHANCE AND ENRICH THE EDUCATIONAL OPPORTUNITIES OF THE SCHOOL'S STUDENTS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </Form990ScheduleAPartVIGrp>
      <Form990ScheduleAPartVIGrp>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>SCHEDULE A, PART IV, SECTION E, LINE 2B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>WITHOUT THE FINANCIAL SUPPORT FROM THE FOUNDATION, IT'S DOUBTFUL THAT THE SCHOOL WOULD HAVE HAD THE FINANCIAL RESOURCES AVAILABLE FOR THE VARIOUS PROGRAM SERVICES PROVIDED. SEE FORM 990, PART III, FOR THE VARIOUS PROGRAM SERVICES PROVIDED DURING THE SCHOOL YEAR.</ExplanationTxt>
      </Form990ScheduleAPartVIGrp>
